# not fixture 02, so not replayed). Blueprint built the page Swatches (14 cards, specs/swatches.yaml); the user picked
# cells in Desktop's own Theme colors grid (10 columns: white, black, then Theme color 1-8, i.e. dataColors[0..7];
# 6 rows) for the cards' own fill, so Desktop wrote the shape; I then hand-wrote ThemeDataColor numbers into the same
# shape (the two candidate sections) to reach ColorId 0/1 (not reachable in the picker) and the range's end.
# Card fills were sampled in the original-resolution captures (local only): see schema.md. The card titles name
# the picker cell they were MEANT for; the user picked other cells for R1 C1 and R1 C2, and the saved JSON is the
# record. Not replayed.

